# No agent attribution

Do not name any coding agent, AI assistant, or tool as an author, co-author, committer, or sign-off on this project.

## Commits

- Use the human operator's existing `user.name` / `user.email` from git config.
- Never pass `--author` for an agent identity.
- Never add `Co-authored-by:` (or similar) lines for Cursor, Copilot, Claude, ChatGPT, Bugbot, or any other agent or bot.
- Never put agent names in the commit subject or body.

## Pull requests

- Write PR titles and bodies as human-authored project prose.
- Never append footers such as "Made with Cursor", "Generated by …", or agent marketing links.
- Never list an agent under Assignees, Reviewers, or as an author in the description.

## Exceptions

Bot accounts that the repository already uses for automation (for example CI bots filing release PRs) stay as they are. This rule is about agent sessions editing this repo, not about disabling existing CI robots.
